<title>PHILIPPINES: FORUM SAYS IN TALKS WITH AIR PHILIPPINES.</title>
<headline>FORUM SAYS IN TALKS WITH AIR PHILIPPINES.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Forum Pacific Inc said on Thursday it was holding talks with Air Philippines Corp for a possible merger.</p>
<p>&quot;The talk is still ongoing,&quot; Forum Pacific president Peter Salud said.</p>
<p>Salud said the plan was first broached up several months ago, but he declined to give any detail regarding the negotiation.</p>
<p>Forum and Air Philippines are both majority owned by businessman William Gatchalian.</p>
<p>Forum, formerly an oil exploration firm, is a newly converted holding company. Air Philippines is one of the newest domestic airlines.</p>
